{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387257-can-somebody-explain-the-limit-on-active-knacks-to-me","id":1387257,"title":"Can somebody explain the limit on active Knacks to me?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-10T05:56:54-07:00","id":1387257,"title":"Can somebody explain the limit on active Knacks to me?","content":"The book says that your dots in Calling limits how many knacks you could have active. How does this work exactly?<br /> <br /> Let's say I have one dot in Trickster and the Knack &quot;In Sheep\u2019s Clothing&quot; that let's me disguise myself without a roll and the Knack &quot;Light Fingered&quot; that lets me steal things from others without needing a roll. I disguise myself with In Sheep's Clothing to get close to a person and decide I need an object of their's which I must steal. If I were to use Light Fingered, must I first drop my use of In Sheep's Clothing before I can do so, showing everyone my true face?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9849,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","user":"Aristarkos","date":". 05-10-2020, 09:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T07:22:42-07:00","id":1387266,"title":"","content":"The number of Active Knack is the number of Knacks you can use in a session.<br /> <br /> You can use the same knack multiple times in the session, but, if you have more knacks than calling dots, you can\u2019t use all callings in the same session.<br /> <br /> In my table, we pick the knacks as we run, so if you have 3 dots in a calling, and 5 knacks from the same calling, you pick 1 in the first scene, and one Immortal in the second scene, you can\u2019t use any other knack for the rest of the session (but can still use the ones you picked before). But, if I am not wrong, by the rules you pick them in the beginning of the session, and is limited to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T08:54:58-07:00","id":1387281,"title":"","content":"As I understand it you can have as many knacks active as you have dots in the appropriate Calling, with Immortal knacks counting for 2 dots. Being able to switch them out at will feels like it makes that limit kind of arbitrary so I'd go with per session. Or hard mode, go with boon rules and only switch them out on a legend up (As I briefly thought was the case <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26056-cassiecataria","name":"CassieCataria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26056_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T09:42:00-07:00","id":1387290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CassieCataria</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387257-can-somebody-explain-the-limit-on-active-knacks-to-me?p=1387281#post1387281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or hard mode, go with boon rules and only switch them out on a legend up (As I briefly thought was the case <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />).</div> </div> </div> </div>In that case, it is useless to have more Knacks than calling dots (what, to me, kind of make sense).<br /> <br /> The problem here is, already too many of the horizontal differences between characters are essentially linked to legend (the vertical aspect of evolution). If you are planning to go a entire campaign without going above Hero, you have characters that have a narrow space to evolve (only skills and attributes).<br /> <br /> (what brings me back to... Edges)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T17:36:33-07:00","id":1387371,"title":"","content":"There's a suggested alternate rule for assigning your Knacks that I prefer to use. Your Knack Slots start each session 'Open', but once you declare a Knack, it's 'locked in' until the end of the session.<br /> <br /> Your Example: Your Trickster Knack Slot starts open, and for the moment you don't have any Knacks. But then you declare that you're going to Disguise yourself, and thus you're using In Sheep's Clothing. Thus, &quot;In Sheep's Clothing&quot; is declared and is now 'taking up' your Trickster Knack Slot. It will remain that way for the rest of the Session.<br /> <br /> And if Players REALLY want to swap out on the fly due to an emergency situation (as a GM I advise against springing a trick to 'catch' your players when they're not specced with their Asskicking Knacks due to it being a Dick Move) then consider allowing them to, if they've filled their slots, spend a point of Momentum for an emergency respec.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T05:34:25-07:00","id":1387457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387257-can-somebody-explain-the-limit-on-active-knacks-to-me?p=1387371#post1387371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a suggested alternate rule for assigning your Knacks that I prefer to use. Your Knack Slots start each session 'Open', but once you declare a Knack, it's 'locked in' until the end of the session.<br /> <br /> Your Example: Your Trickster Knack Slot starts open, and for the moment you don't have any Knacks. But then you declare that you're going to Disguise yourself, and thus you're using In Sheep's Clothing. Thus, &quot;In Sheep's Clothing&quot; is declared and is now 'taking up' your Trickster Knack Slot. It will remain that way for the rest of the Session.<br /> <br /> And if Players REALLY want to swap out on the fly due to an emergency situation (as a GM I advise against springing a trick to 'catch' your players when they're not specced with their Asskicking Knacks due to it being a Dick Move) then consider allowing them to, if they've filled their slots, spend a point of Momentum for an emergency respec.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like this version a lot, I'm going to use it.<br /> <br /> In that case if a player spends momentum to switch Knacks, would you have the effects of the original Knack end instantly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T09:33:02-07:00","id":1387517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387257-can-somebody-explain-the-limit-on-active-knacks-to-me?p=1387457#post1387457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I like this version a lot, I'm going to use it.<br /> <br /> In that case if a player spends momentum to switch Knacks, would you have the effects of the original Knack end instantly?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's what i'd do. Unless in the respec they choose to keep the Knack, of course","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T01:10:53-07:00","id":1393753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387257-can-somebody-explain-the-limit-on-active-knacks-to-me?p=1387371#post1387371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a suggested alternate rule for assigning your Knacks that I prefer to use. Your Knack Slots start each session 'Open', but once you declare a Knack, it's 'locked in' until the end of the session.<br /> <br /> Your Example: Your Trickster Knack Slot starts open, and for the moment you don't have any Knacks. But then you declare that you're going to Disguise yourself, and thus you're using In Sheep's Clothing. Thus, &quot;In Sheep's Clothing&quot; is declared and is now 'taking up' your Trickster Knack Slot. It will remain that way for the rest of the Session.<br /> <br /> And if Players REALLY want to swap out on the fly due to an emergency situation (as a GM I advise against springing a trick to 'catch' your players when they're not specced with their Asskicking Knacks due to it being a Dick Move) then consider allowing them to, if they've filled their slots, spend a point of Momentum for an emergency respec.</div> </div> </div> </div>Going to use this rule too as soon as my group does the upgrade to 2e (still in the middle of a 1e story)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11025-ganruy","name":"Ganruy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T06:43:39-07:00","id":1396667,"title":"","content":"I've actually started to use the House Rule that if they want to change their Knacks, they have to spend a point of Legend. This makes it flexible enough that they don't feel like it's useless having extra Knacks, but gives it enough of a cost that it's a decision they have to think about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7550-vulcan7200","name":"Vulcan7200","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T10:45:43-07:00","id":1396693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vulcan7200</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387257-can-somebody-explain-the-limit-on-active-knacks-to-me?p=1396667#post1396667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've actually started to use the House Rule that if they want to change their Knacks, they have to spend a point of Legend. This makes it flexible enough that they don't feel like it's useless having extra Knacks, but gives it enough of a cost that it's a decision they have to think about.</div> </div> </div> </div>A point of LEGEND? Wow, that's fucking pricy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T11:11:56-07:00","id":1396697,"title":"","content":"According to the books, a Hero can have a number of active knacks equal to their total of Calling dots. In Origin, under Tweaks, it says you can swap out an active knack for an inactive knack in between sessions. So, if you have 5 dots of Callings and 7 knacks, you can only have 5 active at a time, and in between sessions, you can swap out one active one for one of the two extra knacks you have.<br /> <br /> Charging a point of Legend to swap knacks means an Origin character could never swap knacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T13:39:56-07:00","id":1396719,"title":"","content":"I don't think Kyman meant &quot;permanent&quot; Legend. I don't have my books to hand but I think Kyman meant temporary Legend. I may have my terms wrong, but I know that Permanent Legend gives you temporary points to activate your Purviews etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T15:16:37-07:00","id":1396739,"title":"","content":"The problem of spending Legend to change Purviews is that Legend costs a fatebinding or a sacrifice. It means you may take a session just to swap a knack that you may swap in the end of it.<br /> <br /> While I agree moving from \u201cyou can\u2019t\u201d to \u201cit\u2019s very expensive\u201d is a thing, it\u2019s too expensive to worth, so it\u2019s basically useless to set this rule as no one would use it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T23:32:26-07:00","id":1396827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387257-can-somebody-explain-the-limit-on-active-knacks-to-me?p=1396719#post1396719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think Kyman meant &quot;permanent&quot; Legend. I don't have my books to hand but I think Kyman meant temporary Legend. I may have my terms wrong, but I know that Permanent Legend gives you temporary points to activate your Purviews etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never recommended spending Legend to hot-swap your Knacks. My alternate Ruleset was &quot;Spend MOMENTUM to hot-swap your Knacks on the spot&quot;. My comment of &quot;Wow that's expensive&quot; is because, as Mateus noted, spending a point of Legend just to swap your Knacks is really not worth it considering the Marvels or Boons you could use that Legend for.<br /> <br /> Of course above that I recommend the recommended ruleset suggested in the book. Namely, your Knack slots start empty and you can just Declare your Knacks as needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}